mapping "EMC99.1" source="EMC99" target="SNOMED_CT:119959006" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        SE-mirror sctid
        119959006 = SNOMED CT 119959006 119960001 and sctid 119960001 =, BOTH ACTIVE in RF2 20260701
        (valid_end 2099-12-31, invalid_reason empty, rf2). Crosswalk-confirmed via
        sctid_to_athena_id.tdl (119959006->4002208, 119960001->4002209). Defensible active standard
        targets exist, so the mapping carries no invalid_reason. Target definitions:
        119959006 = surgical reconstruction of the adenoid; 119960001 = surgical reconstruction of the
        tonsil. Why partial / : residual source (= other) + partial decomposition (no single concept
        covers both) + the residual may also capture reconstructive techniques not identical to plain
        (e.g. repair, flaps). 119962009 was considered as a third target but is clinically close to
        119960001 and would over-split; left out to avoid redundancy. Confidence capped at per the
        residual+narrower/partial rubric. | Mirror-only lookup, citation empty.
        """
}
